There is a common misconception that the Tiprasa people have achieved progress only because of reservation benefits. Such claims ignore the rich history, administrative capability, and intellectual contributions of the Tiprasa community over centuries.
History records that the Kingdom of Tripura was governed by 187 Kings, maintaining a functioning system of administration, justice, diplomacy, and governance across generations. Such a long and enduring political tradition could not have been sustained without wisdom, leadership, and institutional capacity.
The contribution of distinguished Tiprasa personalities in the field of law and administration is also noteworthy. Eminent figures such as Thakur Sardacharan Debbarma, Thakur Kalicharan Debbarma, Thakur Radhamohan Debbarma, Thakur Prasanna Kumar Debbarma, and Thakur Mahim Chandra Debbarma successfully served as Judges, Magistrates, and administrators during the royal period. Their service in civil and criminal justice demonstrates the community's long-standing involvement in governance, legal affairs, and public administration.
Every society has produced scholars, leaders, administrators, warriors, artists, and reformers. The Tiprasa community is no exception. Rather than relying on stereotypes, we should examine history, acknowledge achievements, and promote mutual respect among all communities.
True progress comes from education, hard work, and unity. Let us celebrate our heritage with pride while building a future based on knowledge, dignity, and cooperation.
